          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A version of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-tuply+monoidal+n-groupoid"} k-tuply monoidal n-groupoid
            but for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/An-spaces"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_n
                spaces
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#homotopytheoretic Homotopy-theoretic
          %p
            Invoking the homotopy hypothesis, we define a
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              \-tuply associative
              = succeed "-groupoid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            to be an
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_k
                \-
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                \-truncated type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+n-type"} homotopy n-type
            with a multiplication that is associative up to higher homotopies involving up to nn variables.
